  [2026-06-19 22:05:29] PUT(strong, 1 peer down) replica1 -> HTTP 200 [OK]  round_trip=9.6ms  body={"success": true, "replica_id": "", "data": {"key": "y", "value": "99", "version": 1, "updated_by": "replica1", "updated_at": "2026-06-19T18:35:29.117271832Z"}, "latency_ms": 6.073}

── Part C: Strong consistency, replica2 ALSO stopped (quorum impossible) ─
$ docker stop replica2
replica2
$ curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8080/put -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"key":"y","value":"100"}'
  [2026-06-19 22:05:35] PUT(strong, 2 peers down) replica1 -> HTTP 503 [FAIL]  round_trip=5003.5ms  body={"success": false, "replica_id": "", "error": "quorum not reached: quorum not reached: got 0/1 acks, errors: [replica2: HTTP POST to http://replica2:8081/internal/replicate: Post \"http://replica2:8081/internal/replicate\": context deadline exceeded (Client.Timeout exceeded while awaiting headers) replica3: HTTP POST to http://replica3:8082/internal/replicate: Post \"http://replica3:8082/internal/replicate\": context deadline exceeded (Client.Timeout exceeded while awaiting headers)]", "latency_ms": 0}

── Restoring all replicas ────────────────────────────────────────────────
$ docker start replica2
replica2
$ docker start replica3
replica3

── Waiting for all replicas to become healthy ────────────────────────────
$ curl -s 'http://localhost:8080/health'
  [2026-06-19 22:05:37] HEALTH replica1 -> HTTP 200 [OK]  round_trip=1.7ms  body={"replica": "replica1", "status": "ok", "time": "2026-06-19T18:35:37Z"}
$ curl -s 'http://localhost:8081/health'
  [2026-06-19 22:05:37] HEALTH replica2 -> HTTP 200 [OK]  round_trip=1.5ms  body={"replica": "replica2", "status": "ok", "time": "2026-06-19T18:35:37Z"}
$ curl -s 'http://localhost:8082/health'
  [2026-06-19 22:05:37] HEALTH replica3 -> HTTP 200 [OK]  round_trip=1.6ms  body={"replica": "replica3", "status": "ok", "time": "2026-06-19T18:35:37Z"}

── Result summary ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Eventual mode, 1 peer down: PUT still succeeded (True), replica3 caught up after restart: False (no retry mechanism, so this is expected to be False).
  Strong mode, 1 peer down (quorum 2/3 reachable): PUT succeeded = True
  Strong mode, 2 peers down (quorum impossible): PUT correctly failed = True
